h-to-node=3D"6"><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"7">2. The Sync Logic Strategy</h3>=
<p data-path-to-node=3D"8">Since you are using a relational structure, the =
<b data-path-to-node=3D"8" data-index-in-node=3D"48">Order of Operations</b=
> is critical to avoid "Orphan Records" on the server.</p><h4 data-path-to-=
node=3D"9">Offline-First Workflow:</h4><ol start=3D"1" data-path-to-node=3D=
"10"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"10,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"10,0,0" da=
ta-index-in-node=3D"0">Local Save:</b> When the user hits "Save," wrap the =
<code data-path-to-node=3D"10,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"48">Transaction</c=
ode> and all <code data-path-to-node=3D"10,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"68">L=
ineItems</code> in a <b data-path-to-node=3D"10,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"=
83">Local Database Transaction</b>. This ensures that if the app crashes mi=
d-save, you don't end up with a Transaction header but no split items.</p><=
/li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"10,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"10,1,0" dat=
a-index-in-node=3D"0">Connectivity Listener:</b> Use MAUI's <code data-path=
-to-node=3D"10,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"34">Connectivity.Current.Connecti=
vityChanged</code> to trigger the DataSync API.</p></li><li><p data-path-to=
-node=3D"10,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"10,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">A=
tomic Sync:</b></p><ul data-path-to-node=3D"10,2,1"><li><p data-path-to-nod=
e=3D"10,2,1,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"10,2,1,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"=
0">Upload Header First:</b> Push the <code data-path-to-node=3D"10,2,1,0,0"=
 data-index-in-node=3D"30">Transaction</code> record.</p></li><li><p data-p=
ath-to-node=3D"10,2,1,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"10,2,1,1,0" data-index-i=
n-node=3D"0">Upload Children:</b> Push the <code data-path-to-node=3D"10,2,=
1,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"26">TransactionLineItem</code> records.</p></l=
i><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"10,2,1,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"10,2,1,2,=
0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Batching:</b> Ideally, the DocUnits Toolkit all=
ows sending the entire "Graph" (Header + Items) in one JSON payload to the =
server's sync endpoint.</p></li></ul></li></ol><hr data-path-to-node=3D"11"=
><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"12">3. Handling the "Split" UI with GUIDs</h3><p =
data-path-to-node=3D"13">In your ViewModel, when the user clicks "Add Split=
," you will instantiate a new <code data-path-to-node=3D"13" data-index-in-=
node=3D"80">TransactionLineItem</code> and immediately assign its <code dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"13" data-index-in-node=3D"127">TransactionId</code> to th=
e <code data-path-to-node=3D"13" data-index-in-node=3D"148">Id</code> of th=
e current Transaction being edited.</p><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"14">4. Impl=
ementation Checklist for Sync</h3><ul data-path-to-node=3D"15"><li><p data-=
path-to-node=3D"15,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"15,0,0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"0">Conflict Resolution:</b> What happens if the user edits the same spe=
nding on two devices? (Usually, "Last Write Wins" based on a <code data-pat=
h-to-node=3D"15,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"125">LastModified</code> timesta=
mp).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"15,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"15=
,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Idempotency:</b> Ensure that if a sync fails=
