"5,1,0">Change the "Show output from:" dropdown at the top of that window t=
o <b data-path-to-node=3D"5,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"69">Build</b>.</p></=
li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"5,2,0">Scroll to the bottom and look for the=
 red text or the specific <code data-path-to-node=3D"5,2,0" data-index-in-n=
ode=3D"63">error CS...</code>.</p></li></ol><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"6">Ste=
p 2: The 3 most common culprits for this MAUI trick</h3><p data-path-to-nod=
e=3D"7">Based on what usually breaks when isolating a MAUI app to Windows-o=
nly, check these three things:</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"8"><b data-path-t=
o-node=3D"8" data-index-in-node=3D"0">1. You are missing the Design package=
.</b>
EF Core absolutely requires a specific package to generate code at design-t=
ime. If it's missing, the background build fails.</p><ul data-path-to-node=
=3D"9"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"9,0,0">Ensure <b data-path-to-node=3D"9,=
0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"7"><code data-path-to-node=3D"9,0,0" data-index-=
in-node=3D"7">Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design</code></b> is installed =
in your <code data-path-to-node=3D"9,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"65">Purse</=
code> (MAUI) project.</p></li></ul><p data-path-to-node=3D"10"><b data-path=
-to-node=3D"10" data-index-in-node=3D"0">2. Duplicate XML Tags in <code dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"10" data-index-in-node=3D"25">.csproj</code></b>
