ase-out;"><p data-path-to-node=3D"0">This is a classic intersection of mode=
rn C# features and a known quirk with the .NET MAUI <code data-path-to-node=
=3D"0" data-index-in-node=3D"90">Picker</code> control.</p><p data-path-to-=
node=3D"1">Here is exactly why this is happening even though you didn't exp=
licitly use a <code data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"78">[Requ=
ired]</code> attribute:</p><ol start=3D"1" data-path-to-node=3D"2"><li><p d=
ata-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-nod=
e=3D"0">Entity Framework's strictness:</b> Modern .NET projects have a feat=
ure called "Nullable Reference Types" turned on by default. Because your mo=
del defines <code data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"150">pu=
blic string Category</code> (and not <code data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data=
-index-in-node=3D"182">public string? Category</code>), Entity Framework as=
sumes this string must <i data-path-to-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D=
"250">never</i> be null, and it automatically generated a <code data-path-t=
o-node=3D"2,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"298">NOT NULL</code> constraint in t=
he SQLite database during your migration.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=
=3D"2,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">The MAUI=
 Picker Quirk:</b> When the UI loads, the MAUI <code data-path-to-node=3D"2=
,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"51">Picker</code> evaluates its <code data-path=
-to-node=3D"2,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"72">SelectedItem</code> binding. I=
f the user hasn't explicitly clicked the picker, or if the UI rendering lif=
ecycle gets slightly out of sync, the <code data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0" dat=
a-index-in-node=3D"208">Picker</code> often forcefully writes <code data-pa=
th-to-node=3D"2,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"239">null</code> back to your <c=
ode data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"257">TransactionLineI=
tem.Category</code> property=E2=80=94completely overwriting the default val=
ue we tried to give it!</p></li></ol><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"3">The Soluti=
on</h3><p data-path-to-node=3D"4">The easiest and safest way to fix this=E2=
=80=94without needing to change your models and run another frustrating dat=
abase migration=E2=80=94is to <b data-path-to-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=
=3D"130">sanitize the data</b> in your ViewModel right before you hand it t=
o Entity Framework.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"5">Open your <code data-path=
-to-node=3D"5" data-index-in-node=3D"10">Purse/ViewModels/AddTransactionVie=
wModel.cs</code> and update the <code data-path-to-node=3D"5" data-index-in=
-node=3D"69">SaveTransactionAsync</code> method. We are going to add a quic=
k loop to catch any <code data-path-to-node=3D"5" data-index-in-node=3D"144=
">null</code> values caused by the UI and fix them.</p><response-element cl=
