uration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: ease-out;"><p data-path-to-node=
=3D"0">You are 100% right. I gave you a band-aid when you needed a cure, an=
d you caught it perfectly.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"1">The sanitization l=
oop was a hack to cover up the fact that the two-way data binding was faili=
ng. Because <code data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"105">Transa=
ctionLineItem</code> is a plain class, when we loaded an existing transacti=
on from the database and populated the <code data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-i=
ndex-in-node=3D"218">Splits</code> collection, the UI <code data-path-to-no=
de=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"244">Picker</code> had no idea the <code dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"267">Category</code> property wa=
s set, defaulted to <code data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"307=
">null</code>, and overwrote our database value.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D=
"2">You=E2=80=99ve hit a classic architectural dilemma in MAUI: <b data-pat=
h-to-node=3D"2" data-index-in-node=3D"52">How do we make our models observa=
ble without polluting our shared server library with UI frameworks?</b></p>=
<p data-path-to-node=3D"3">Because <code data-path-to-node=3D"3" data-index=
-in-node=3D"8">TransactionLineItem</code> already inherits from <code data-=
path-to-node=3D"3" data-index-in-node=3D"50">OfflineClientEntity</code> (wh=
ich inherits from the server toolkit's base class), we cannot inherit from =
<code data-path-to-node=3D"3" data-index-in-node=3D"148">ObservableObject</=
code> (C# doesn't allow multiple base classes).</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"=
4">The correct, professional fix is to manually implement <code data-path-t=
o-node=3D"4" data-index-in-node=3D"55">INotifyPropertyChanged</code> on you=
r shared models using standard C#.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"5">Here is th=
e exact step-by-step fix to rip out the hack and fix the bindings at the ro=
ot.</p><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"6">Step 1: Update <code data-path-to-node=
=3D"6" data-index-in-node=3D"15">TransactionLineItem.cs</code> (in <code da=
ta-path-to-node=3D"6" data-index-in-node=3D"42">Purse.Shared</code>)</h3><p=
 data-path-to-node=3D"7">We will implement <code data-path-to-node=3D"7" da=
ta-index-in-node=3D"18">INotifyPropertyChanged</code> manually. This requir=
es zero extra NuGet packages, keeping your shared library perfectly clean f=
or the ASP.NET Core server.</p><response-element class=3D"" ng-version=3D"0=
