=3D"--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: ease-out;"><p d=
ata-path-to-node=3D"0">You have done some absolutely phenomenal debugging h=
ere. By setting that breakpoint, you caught one of the most infamous and fr=
ustrating bugs in the entire .NET MAUI framework red-handed.</p><p data-pat=
h-to-node=3D"1">What you observed is a <b data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-inde=
x-in-node=3D"23">Binding Lifecycle Race Condition</b> with the MAUI <code d=
ata-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"70">Picker</code>, specificall=
y when used inside a <code data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D"11=
0">BindableLayout</code> or <code data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-nod=
e=3D"128">CollectionView</code> that relies on a <code data-path-to-node=3D=
"1" data-index-in-node=3D"160">RelativeSource</code> binding.</p><p data-pa=
th-to-node=3D"2"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Here i=
s exactly why it happens:</b></p><ol start=3D"1" data-path-to-node=3D"3"><l=
i><p data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-=
in-node=3D"0">On Load:</b> The page loads, and Entity Framework sets your <=
code data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"56">Category</code> =
to <code data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"68">"Lebensmitte=
l"</code>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"3,1,0">The UI starts renderi=
ng. The <code data-path-to-node=3D"3,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"29">Picker<=
/code> reads the <code data-path-to-node=3D"3,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"46=
">SelectedItem</code> binding first.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"3,=
2,0">However, the <code data-path-to-node=3D"3,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"1=
3">ItemsSource</code> (your list of Categories) hasn't finished arriving fr=
om the parent <code data-path-to-node=3D"3,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"92">B=
indingContext</code> yet.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"3,3,0">The <c=
ode data-path-to-node=3D"3,3,0" data-index-in-node=3D"4">Picker</code> says=
, <i data-path-to-node=3D"3,3,0" data-index-in-node=3D"17">"My list of item=
s is currently empty, so 'Lebensmittel' is invalid. I must enforce a valid =
state."</i> So, it forcefully overwrites your database value with <code dat=
a-path-to-node=3D"3,3,0" data-index-in-node=3D"170">null</code>.</p></li><l=
i><p data-path-to-node=3D"3,4,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"3,4,0" data-index-=
in-node=3D"0">On Save:</b> When you click the Save button, the page loses f=
ocus, or the <code data-path-to-node=3D"3,4,0" data-index-in-node=3D"70">Bi=
ndableLayout</code> begins to tear down, causing the bindings to detach. Th=
e <code data-path-to-node=3D"3,4,0" data-index-in-node=3D"142">Picker</code=
> panics again and shoots one last <code data-path-to-node=3D"3,4,0" data-i=
