"8,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">When <code data-path-to-node=3D"8,0,0" dat=
a-index-in-node=3D"5">SafeSelectedItem</code> arrives first:</b> <code data=
-path-to-node=3D"8,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"37">SyncSelection()</code> is=
 called, sees <code data-path-to-node=3D"8,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"69">I=
temsSource</code> is null, and does nothing. The property is safely cached =
in memory.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"8,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=
=3D"8,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">When <code data-path-to-node=3D"8,1,0" =
data-index-in-node=3D"5">ItemsSource</code> arrives second:</b> <code data-=
path-to-node=3D"8,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"33">OnPropertyChanged</code> f=
ires for the source. It queues <code data-path-to-node=3D"8,1,0" data-index=
-in-node=3D"83">SyncSelection()</code> via the Dispatcher. By the time it e=
xecutes, the native list is fully built, <code data-path-to-node=3D"8,1,0" =
data-index-in-node=3D"176">items.Contains()</code> evaluates to true, and i=
t assigns the value.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"8,2,0"><b data-pat=
h-to-node=3D"8,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">When MAUI wipes the control:</=
b> If a lifecycle event causes the native <code data-path-to-node=3D"8,2,0"=
 data-index-in-node=3D"68">Picker</code> to suddenly drop its selection to =
<code data-path-to-node=3D"8,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"109">null</code>, <=
code data-path-to-node=3D"8,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"115">Scenario C</cod=
e> catches it. Because <code data-path-to-node=3D"8,2,0" data-index-in-node=
=3D"146">SafeSelectedItem</code> still holds the truth, it dispatches a com=
mand to immediately push the value back onto the screen.</p></li></ol><p da=
ta-path-to-node=3D"9">Using <code data-path-to-node=3D"9" data-index-in-nod=
e=3D"6">Dispatcher.Dispatch</code> prevents the dreaded infinite loops that=
 often plague <code data-path-to-node=3D"9" data-index-in-node=3D"80">TwoWa=
y</code> binding overrides, making this custom control safe to use anywhere=
