de=3D"193">*ViewModel</code>, and automatically registers them as Transient=
s, completely eliminating boilerplate DI code!)</i></p><h3 data-path-to-nod=
e=3D"5">2. Localization</h3><ul data-path-to-node=3D"6"><li><p data-path-to=
-node=3D"6,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"6,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Zer=
o Hardcoded Strings:</b> Every piece of text in XAML or C# will reference <=
code data-path-to-node=3D"6,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"73">AppResources</co=
de>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"6,1,0">In XAML, it will look like =
<code data-path-to-node=3D"6,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"27">Text=3D"{x:Stat=
ic AppResources.YourKey}"</code> (assuming the namespace is globally define=
d).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"6,2,0">In C#, it will be standard s=
tatic access: <code data-path-to-node=3D"6,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"42">A=
ppResources.YourKey</code>.</p></li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"7">3. XAM=
